      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic static image and visual understanding task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file detect_image_labels.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_labels.py - detects labels or objects in a static image\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] describe_image.py - generates a short visual description for an image\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_text.py - detects text appearing inside an image\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] score_image_safety.py - checks an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] vision_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Static Image and Visual Understanding\n6. [HELPER] vision_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Static Image and Visual Understanding\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] image_summary.py - Summarize visual analysis results\n8. [LATER-STEP] alt_text_translate.py - Translate generated image descriptions\n9. [LATER-STEP] visual_safety_text.py - Check generated visual labels for unsafe text\n10. [LATER-STEP] image_asset_archive.py - Archive image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
